sweet usb: survive a second enumeration (0220).

all-14 (2026-11-18): a VM on the Mac took the phone's USB device and released it again. The Mac enumerated it a second time
(bus reset, address 2, configured), en3 appeared but stayed "inactive"; the last request was CLEAR_FEATURE(ENDPOINT_HALT) for
0x82. The driver kept the first configuration: SET_CONFIGURATION returned early, the old transfers and data toggles stayed, and
the NETWORK_CONNECTION notification went out with a toggle the host no longer expected.
Now, as Linux dwc3 (gadget.c dwc3_gadget_reset_interrupt / dwc3_stop_active_transfers, core.h command values from
android_kernel_xiaomi_spes): bus reset, disconnect and SET_CONFIGURATION(0) end the running transfers on the three data
endpoints (End Transfer with the resource index read back after Start Transfer), disable them and forget the configuration;
the next SET_CONFIGURATION sets them up afresh. CLEAR_FEATURE(ENDPOINT_HALT) on a data endpoint issues Clear Stall (toggle
reset). Completions that arrive for an unconfigured device are dropped. No change before the first configuration.
Not run on hardware yet.

